From 93e6cfed57370548723788bae9a139f2b6aeee82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yonglunyao <yonglunyao@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:09:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] arm64: dts: qcom: add Huawei MateBook E Go (gaokun3)
 board

Import the gaokun3 board DTS from linux-gaokun-buildbot (0099 b-side,
blob 94e7eeb7e) and adapt it for the OpenHarmony 6.6.101 baseline,
per docs/m1/dts-gap.md:

- camera dtsi not imported (out of scope for the OH port)
- DSI overlays compiled out (#if 0): OH 6.6 drm-msm has no sc8280xp
  DSI stack and no DSI clock IDs in qcom,dispcc-sc8280xp.h; simpledrm
  provides the framebuffer until the M2 backport
- cooling-device references renamed cpu4-7 -> CPU4-7 (6.6 upper-case)
- base nodes absent from OH 6.6.101 sc8280xp.dtsi added at board level
  (lifted verbatim from mainline v7.2-rc2, the buildbot CI baseline):
  gpi_dma0/1/2 (gpi.c fallback compat present in 6.6), usb_2 + mp
  dwc3 child, pcie4_port0 bridge (WCN6855 WiFi hard dependency),
  remoteproc_slpi + smp2p-slpi + pil_slpi_mem (kept disabled per the
  M0 decision), usb_0/1_dwc3_hs role-switch endpoints (port@0 only),
  dmic23 pinctrl states
- sc8280xp.dtsi / sc8280xp-pmics.dtsi untouched

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts | 2127 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 2127 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts

